{"name":"Pendula Garden","hex":"#7b8267","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pendula","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of pendulum"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pendula"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pendulum","blocks":[{"text":"A pendulum is a mechanical device consisting of a weight suspended from a pivot so that it can swing freely. When a pendulum is displaced sideways from its resting mechanical equilibrium position, it is subject to a restoring force due to gravity, which will accelerate it back toward the equilibrium position. When released, the restoring force acting on the pendulum's mass causes it to oscillate about the equilibrium position, swinging back and forth. The time for one complete cycle, a left swing and a right swing, or frequency, is commonly known as its \"period\". The period depends both on the length of the pendulum and, somewhat, on the amplitude. The SI unit of the period of a pendulum is the second (s)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Simple_gravity_pendulum.svg/330px-Simple_gravity_pendulum.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pendulum"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fa/PenduloTmg.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fa/PenduloTmg.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APenduloTmg.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Oscillating_pendulum.gif/330px-Oscillating_pendulum.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Oscillating_pendulum.gif/330px-Oscillating_pendulum.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOscillating_pendulum.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Pendulum_30deg.gif/120px-Pendulum_30deg.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/Pendulum_30deg.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Pendulum_30deg.gif/120px-Pendulum_30deg.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APendulum_30deg.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Pendulum_60deg.gif/120px-Pendulum_60deg.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte